.TH playmp3 1 "FUZIX System Utilities" "FUZIX"
.SH NAME
playmp3, playwav, playflac \- play a sound file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B playmp3
.I file.mp3
[\fIvolume\fR]
.br
.B playwav
.I file.wav
[\fIvolume\fR]
.br
.B playflac
.I file.flac
[\fIvolume\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Each of these decodes its kind of file and plays it, printing the sample
rate, the number of channels and the volume as it starts.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I volume
0 to 100.  The default is 80.
.SH RUNNING IN THE BACKGROUND
Put an
.B &
after the command and the shell gives you the prompt back while it
plays.  Note the process id the shell prints if you want to stop it
early;
.B kill
takes that number, not a job number.
.SH NOTES
Only one player may hold the sound device at a time.  Starting a second
while one is playing gets an error, not a mix.
.PP
Decoding an MP3 is real work for this machine.  It keeps up, but a
compile running beside it will make it stutter.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR playmod (1),
.BR kill (1),
.BR ps (1)
